    <div class="rc-title">Potato Attacks Comparison</div>
    <div class="rc-desc">PrintSpoofer vs JuicyPotato vs GodPotato vs SweetPotato — when to use which, OS compatibility, and current bypass status.</div>
    <span class="rc-arrow">→</span>
  </a>
  <a href="/research/responder-ntlmrelay" class="research-card" data-cat="ad">
    <div class="rc-tag ad">Active Directory</div>
    <div class="rc-title">Responder + NTLMRelayx Chain</div>
    <div class="rc-desc">LLMNR/NBT-NS poisoning → relay → SMB signing disabled targets → shell or DA hash. Full attack chain with edge cases.</div>
    <span class="rc-arrow">→</span>
  </a>
  <a href="/research/amsi-bypass" class="research-card" data-cat="evasion">
    <div class="rc-tag evasion">Evasion</div>
    <div class="rc-title">AMSI Bypass Techniques (2026)</div>
    <div class="rc-desc">Working PowerShell AMSI patches, memory patching via reflection, CLM bypass, and constrained language mode escapes.</div>
    <span class="rc-arrow">→</span>
  </a>
  <a href="/research/gpo-abuse" class="research-card" data-cat="ad">
    <div class="rc-tag ad">Active Directory</div>
    <div class="rc-title">GPO Abuse for Persistence</div>
