  <a href="/research/certipy" class="research-card" data-cat="ad">
    <div class="rc-tag ad">Active Directory</div>
    <div class="rc-title">Certipy Complete Guide</div>
    <div class="rc-desc">Full Certipy workflow: find, req, auth, shadow, relay, forge — all subcommands with real-world output examples.</div>
    <span class="rc-arrow">→</span>
  </a>
  <a href="/research/shadow-credentials" class="research-card" data-cat="ad">
    <div class="rc-tag ad">Active Directory</div>
    <div class="rc-title">Shadow Credentials Attack</div>
    <div class="rc-desc">msDS-KeyCredentialLink manipulation via Whisker/Certipy → PKINIT → TGT → NT hash without password reset.</div>
    <span class="rc-arrow">→</span>
  </a>
  <a href="/research/nfs-exploitation" class="research-card" data-cat="web">
    <div class="rc-tag web">Infrastructure</div>
    <div class="rc-title">NFS Exploitation</div>
    <div class="rc-desc">no_root_squash UID spoofing, SUID binary planting, squashfs tricks, and NFS version fingerprinting for privesc.</div>
    <span class="rc-arrow">→</span>
  </a>
  <a href="/research/container-escape" class="research-card" data-cat="priv">
    <div class="rc-tag priv">Privilege Escalation</div>
    <div class="rc-title">Docker / LXD Container Escape</div>
    <div class="rc-desc">Privileged container escapes, cgroup release_agent, LXD image trick, socket mounts, and cap_sys_admin abuse.</div>
    <span class="rc-arrow">→</span>
  </a>
  <a href="/research/credential-hunting" class="research-card" data-cat="tools">
    <div class="rc-tag tools">Tools & Setup</div>
    <div class="rc-title">Credential Hunting Scripts</div>
    <div class="rc-desc">Automated one-liners for Linux/Windows credential discovery — config files, env vars, history, browsers, keyrings.</div>
    <span class="rc-arrow">→</span>
  </a>
</div>

<script>
function filterTopics(cat) {
  document.querySelectorAll('.filter-btn').forEach(b => b.classList.remove('active'));
  event.target.classList.add('active');
  document.querySelectorAll('.research-card').forEach(card => {
    card.style.display = (cat === 'all' || card.dataset.cat === cat) ? 'block' : 'none';
  });
}
</script>
